# Deployment build artifacts.
#
# These are produced by the builders and the validator during the GitHub Pages
# deploy, and are deliberately NOT committed: a checkout must never carry a
# deployment snapshot, or a developer would be reading stale published evidence
# while believing it is current. A local checkout therefore runs on the small
# curated fallback in data/snapshot_poi.json, which the UI labels
# "SNAPSHOT SAMPLE". See docs/DATA_PROVENANCE.md.
#
# data/pedestrian_activity.json is NOT listed here: its unavailable-state stub is
# committed on purpose, so the repository ships an explicit "no evidence" state
# rather than a missing file. Running the builder overwrites it locally; restore
# it with `git checkout -- data/pedestrian_activity.json` before committing.
data/runtime_poi.json
data/deployment_manifest.json

# Python bytecode from running the test suite or the builders.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
node_modules/

# Gate L (#65) research cache. The audit scripts stream the official legacy
# BIFF8 .xls editions and the ArcGIS geometry into this directory to fingerprint
# and parse them. Raw third-party files are never committed; only the compact
# normalized JSON reports under research/urban_planning_gate/results/ are. See
# research/urban_planning_gate/README.md.
research/urban_planning_gate/cache/
